  "hypothetical_terms": 49,
  "method": "exact recursive section caps plus the block erasure relation lemma; two Ferrers DPs and exhaustive integer-partition audit",
  "n": 7,
  "proof_formula": "For X=direct_sum U_i, K=ker(X->H), W=E_d subset H, and a block J with complement S, dim(W intersect U_S) >= dim(W)-r_J+dim(proj_J K). Hence a section cap dim(W intersect U_S)<=dim(W)-c(J) gives dim(proj_J K)<=r_J-c(J). Summing over a partition of the 49 indices gives dim H>=sum_J c(J). More strongly, if a family of blocks covers each coordinate t times, the block row-echelon (linear Shearer) inequality gives t*dim(K)<=sum_J dim(proj_J K), hence dim(H)>=(sum_J c(J))/t.",
